From: GBRUNCH
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu6: do not offer packed RAW formats on IPU4P

On IPU4P the CSI-2 packed RAW10/RAW12 capture formats use a MIPI output pin
(IPU4P_FW_ISYS_PIN_TYPE_MIPI). With the Surface Pro 7's 4-lane rear ov8865 such
a stream opens and starts but never gets a frame start, and stopping it times
out; libcamera picked the packed format for the camera's video mode
(1632x1224 SBGGR10P, stride 2048) and the unpacked one for photos (SBGGR10,
stride 3264, RAW_SOC pin), which works, as it does on the front camera
(GBRUNCH, 2026-11-10). Leave the packed formats out of VIDIOC_ENUM_FMT on
IPU4P so userspace chooses the unpacked ones.

--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c	2026-11-10 21:34:38.840385243 +0900
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c	2026-11-10 21:34:38.853821056 +0900
@@ -167,6 +167,8 @@
 static int ipu6_isys_vidioc_enum_fmt(struct file *file, void *fh,
 				     struct v4l2_fmtdesc *f)
 {
+	struct ipu6_isys_video *av = video_drvdata(file);
+	bool ipu4p = IS_IPU4P(av->isys->adev->isp);
 	unsigned int i, num_found;
 
 	for (i = 0, num_found = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(ipu6_isys_pfmts); i++) {
@@ -176,6 +178,18 @@
 		     f->type != V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE))
 			continue;
 
+		/*
+		 * GBRUNCH: IPU4P stores the CSI-2 packed RAW10/RAW12 formats
+		 * through a MIPI output pin, which delivered no frames from the
+		 * Surface Pro 7's 4-lane rear camera (the stream starts, no
+		 * SOF ever arrives); the unpacked RAW16 formats (RAW_SOC pin)
+		 * work on both cameras. Do not offer the packed ones.
+		 */
+		if (ipu4p && !ipu6_isys_pfmts[i].is_meta &&
+		    ipu6_isys_pfmts[i].bpp == ipu6_isys_pfmts[i].bpp_packed &&
+		    ipu6_isys_pfmts[i].bpp_packed > 8)
+			continue;
+
 		if (f->mbus_code && f->mbus_code != ipu6_isys_pfmts[i].code)
 			continue;
 
